    "updated_at": "2022-12-05T03:03:31Z",
    "body": "Does the portion of the linked spec\r\n\r\n> (And, as usual for tree-scoped references, continuing up to the host’s tree if needed.)\r\n\r\n(which I don't really have the background to understand) have any implications here? It seems like maybe the algorithm is more complex than just finding the element with the ID, and actually needs to do some extra tree-crawling? If that's the case, extracting out HTML's algorithm doesn't seem quite right...",
